# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in the key:
#
#     cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
#
# backend/.env is gitignored, so it is NEVER carried by a branch, a clone or a
# merge — every machine has to create its own. If the agent features report
# "No OPENAI_API_KEY configured", this is the file that is missing.
#
# The key is read server-side in app/agents/client.py and never reaches the
# browser. Do not put it in any VITE_* variable: everything Vite inlines ships
# to the client.

# Required by the agent-backed features: Investigations (the whole module),
# Promotion Intelligence's "Go deeper" analysis, and Decision Center's AI
# Decision Brief. The rest of Promotion Intelligence — facts, KPIs and charts —
# is computed from the star schema and works without a key.
#
# DECISION CENTER DOES NOT NEED THIS KEY. The decision record, its figures, the
# recommendation, the risk assessment, Save Decision and the report are all
# computed server-side and never call OpenAI. Without a key the AI Decision
# Brief card says it is not configured and every other part of the page works
# exactly as it does with one.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to gpt-4o-mini when unset.
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Optional. Any provider that speaks the OpenAI chat-completions protocol works
# here. To use Grok instead of OpenAI, put an xAI key in OPENAI_API_KEY and set:
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.x.ai/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=grok-4-fast-non-reasoning
